    <DocumentationNarrative Id="source:cli:meta-weave:app:narrative:guide" DocumentationSubjectId="source:cli:meta-weave:app" PreviousNarrativeId="source:cli:meta-weave:app:narrative:summary">
      <Body>MetaWeave is model-to-model conversion for Meta workspaces. A MetaWeave workspace is a first-class correspondence between two workspace contracts. It contains the independent directions that are supported, the requirements for entering each direction, and the transformations that populate target entities.

The correspondence is the authored conversion truth. It is ordinary Meta workspace data, so it remains inspectable, versionable, and representation-neutral rather than being hidden inside handwritten converter code.

## WeaveScript is modeled transformation

WeaveScript is a modeled language for transforming models, distilled from MetaTransformScript and deliberately bounded to workspace conversion. Its recognizable T-SQL-shaped text is an authoring and inspection surface, not a collection of stored scripts. The MetaWeave workspace contains the typed semantic query graph that the text represents.

MetaWeave executes that graph directly with its in-memory relational engine. It does not send conversion queries to SQL Server. SQL remains available as one workspace representation alongside XML and C#.

A direction requirement is a violation query: zero rows satisfy it, while every returned row becomes a concrete diagnostic with projected evidence. All requirements run against the immutable source before target construction starts.

Each transformation projects records for one target entity. MetaWeave derives their execution order from the target model dependency graph, starts with an empty target instance, and submits every insertion through normal Meta Core operations. Every successful operation becomes the next valid target state. The state after the last scheduled transformation is the completed workspace.

## Execute a correspondence

```text
meta-weave execute \
  --workspace &lt;weave-workspace&gt; \
  --source-workspace &lt;populated-source&gt; \
  --target-workspace &lt;target-contract&gt; \
  --xml &lt;new-target-workspace&gt;
```

`forward` is the default direction. The target workspace supplies its model contract, not seed instances. Exactly one of `--xml`, `--csharp`, or `--sql` selects the new workspace representation. A failed requirement or transformation creates no output.

`meta-weave show` summarizes a correspondence. `emit-requirement` and `emit-transformation` render modeled query graphs as readable WeaveScript. Update commands accept replacement text through standard input and store the parsed semantic model back in the same correspondence workspace.</Body>
